3) Decision framework: how to compare settlement vs trial
- Estimate a dollar value for your “case value” (your expected damages). If uncertain, ask your attorney for a low/medium/high damages estimate.
- Estimate your probability of winning (p). Estimate expected recovery at trial = p * damages.
- Subtract expected costs to get to trial (Ctrial) and post‑trial enforcement costs (Ccollect).
- Expected value of trial = (p * damages) - Ctrial - Ccollect.
- Compare that to the certain settlement amount (S) being offered, minus any costs to implement (Csettle, e.g., taxes, structured payment fees).
- Accept settlement if S - Csettle > Expected value of trial (or if you prefer certainty and reduced emotional/time cost).
