- Are any depositions or subpoenas still advisable before the hearing?

Procedural and tactical questions
- Are any dispositive or evidentiary motions appropriate now (summary judgment, motions in limine)?
- Should we try settlement negotiations or mediation before the hearing/trial? Would you recommend private mediation? When?
- If we settle, how will we structure the release and dismissal so we retain remedies if the other side breaches?

Settlement terms to negotiate (ask lawyer about each)
- Total payment amount and schedule (lump sum vs installments)
- Security for payment (escrow, promissory note, lien, confession of judgment if available)
- Confidentiality/non-disparagement clauses (and carve-outs for legal advice)
- Release language (full release of claims vs limited release; include counterclaims)
- Allocation of attorney’s fees and costs (who pays)
- Dismissal with/without prejudice and whether the release includes an agreed judgment
- Tax treatment of settlement (ask about tax consequences or consult accountant)
- Enforcement remedies for breach (interest, fees, enforcement jurisdiction)

Trial-readiness checklist
- Organized exhibit list and exhibit binders (contracts, amendments, emails, bank records, invoices)
- Chronology/timeline of events (one-page summary for court)
- Witness contact info and witness statements or declarations; plan for witness preparation
- Deposition transcripts and key page extracts (flagged for impeachment)
- Expert reports (if necessary) and retention needs
- Trial demonstratives (charts, spreadsheet, timeline)
- Pretrial checklist: motions in limine, exhibit lists, witness lists, proposed findings/jury instructions (if jury), pretrial conference

Documents/evidence you should bring to your meeting
- The complete contract(s) and any amendments, side agreements, or addenda
- All communications: emails, texts, DMs, letters that relate to the dispute (chronologically organized)
- Financial records: invoices, receipts, bank statements, payroll records relevant to damages/loss
- Any prior settlement offers or demand letters
- Proof of performance and proof of breach (if available)
- Deposition transcripts and discovery responses; production log (who produced what)
- Witness names, phone numbers, and short summary of what each will say
- Calendar entries, meeting notes, photos, or other documentary proof
- Any public filings or prior court documents in this case

