- Weak documentary or witness support on key elements
- Very high litigation costs relative to expected recovery
- Opponent has collection problems but you can’t secure payment
- Personal or business reputation risks you want to avoid
- Low probability of recovering full award even if you win

G. Red flags that suggest pushing for trial
- Strong, clear documentary proof and credible witnesses
- Opponent is clearly liable and has ability to pay
- Settlement offers are well below expected recoverable value
- You want a legal precedent or court vindication (non‑monetary priority)
- Opponent is using settlement delay as a stalling tactic

