2) High‑priority questions to ask Robert Kim
A. Case strength & likelihood
- Based on everything discovered, how strong are our legal and factual claims? What are the key strengths and weaknesses?
- What is the realistic probability (in your view) of winning at hearing/trial, expressed as a percentage or range?
- What are the key factual disputes the court will have to resolve?

B. Damages & relief
- What damages or remedies can we reasonably expect if we win (compensatory, consequential, statutory, attorneys’ fees, interest, costs)?
- Are there any caps or offsets the court is likely to apply?
- Can we get attorneys’ fees and costs if we prevail (contract clause, statute)?

