- Full discovery outputs (responses, production, depositions, exhibits).
- All contract(s) at issue and any amendments, emails, text messages, notes reflecting negotiations or performance.
- Evidence of damages (invoices, payroll, lost profits calculations, tax returns if needed).
- Chronology/timeline of events (one‑page timeline is helpful).
- List of potential witnesses with summaries of expected testimony and contact info.
- Any prior settlement communications/offers.
- Financial information about the opposing party (if available) relevant to collectability.

4) Simple decision/economic framework to evaluate offers
- Expected value = Probability of success × Net recovery if you win − Estimated cost to get to verdict.
Example: If lawyer estimates 60% chance to win, likely judgment $50,000, and further costs $15,000:
Expected value = 0.6 × 50,000 − 15,000 = $15,000.
