Assistant: I can help you get organized. Below is a focused checklist of what to prepare and a prioritized set of questions to ask Robert Kim (and to think through yourself) so you can decide whether to accept any settlement offer or push for trial. I also include a short sample email you can send your attorney and a few tactical points to consider.

First: quick clarifying questions for you (so I can tailor anything further)
- Are you the plaintiff or the defendant in this dispute?
- Have you received a settlement offer (written or verbal)? If so, what are the key terms?
